  "actualProductionConnections": [
    "create writes neverStarted; noteUploadIntent durably sets started and clears stale safeCleanup before AFC creation. Old absent history stays unknown.",
    "completeRemoteCleanup derives a persistent pre-submission cleanup summary from the same actual sealed grant/Outcome, binding path/device pin/candidate bytes/hash and Remove+Stop facts.",
    "retireUnsubmitted uses current owner/rawSHA CAS and safe actual history; publishes retirementPending before fixed owned candidate unlink and directory fsync, then publishes retired. No new queue/store/file name is introduced.",
    "resumeRetirement and create re-confirm local absence and directory fsync. A successor retains exactly one predecessor id/revision/rawJSON hash/time, never an accumulating history.",
    "Coordinator.prepare verifies its new archive and lease first, then retires only eligible old state. Actual preparation failure preserves its primary error plus independent retirement result/error.",
    "Coordinator.recover handles actual local pending/retired/interrupted states; safe-cleanup history can retire after restart. Submitted Upgrade/receipt/Lookup remain retained and use the original authenticated recovery only."
  ],
  "cancellationContract": "Before admission/resume, cancellation throws without mutation. After durable pending admission, synchronous cleanup/terminal commit finishes despite later cancellation; I/O errors never mint receipt and leave recoverable state. A new create still checks cancellation before publication.",
  "clockContract": "No scheduler or retry timestamps/backoff added. Existing dates remain finite/nondecreasing; successor creation cannot predate its retained predecessor retirement.",
  "testDefinitionScope": [
    "Actual owned JSON/candidate I/O and raw SHA binding; legacy nil history; three real candidate present/unlinked/synced reopen states; actual chmod/write failure; pre-admission and pending-resume cancellation.",
    "Real original signed unresolved-requirement package forces preparation failure after signing checkpoint, then a valid next package prepares with retirement linkage.",
    "Actual TLS partial upload/fresh authenticated cleanup/reopen retirement/new package preparation and actual Complete or same-version/not-found Lookup refusal definitions."
  ],
  "remaining": [
